llowing:\n\n- If we project the vector $\\overset{\\to }{OP}$ onto the $xy$-plane for every point $P$ on our surface, the resulting vector makes an angle of $2$ radians with the positive $x$-axis. Therefore, we must have $\\theta =2$ for every point on the surface.\n\n- On the other hand, $r$ and $z$ can vary arbitrarily in their respective domains.\n\nTherefore, the equation of the surface in cylindrical polar coordinates is $\\theta =2.$" 13194139534610 true] [17592186298623 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298624 13194139534610 true] [17592186298623 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298625 13194139534610 true] [17592186298623 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298626 13194139534610 true] [17592186298623 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298627 13194139534610 true] [17592186298623 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298628 13194139534610 true] [17592186298623 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534610 true] [17592186298623 1041 "selection" 13194139534610 true] [17592186298623 1104 #edb/ref 17592186298628 13194139534610 true] [17592186298623 1110 #uuid "331d6402-0225-5295-b92d-5dd91e02906a" 13194139534610 true] [17592186298624 1034 "z=2\\theta " 13194139534610 true] [17592186298624 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534610 true] [17592186298624 1111 #uuid "61f10c8b-2921-5587-9e6f-28b52f2b976d" 13194139534610 true] [17592186298625 1034 "\\theta =2r" 13194139534610 true] [17592186298625 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534610 true] [17592186298625 1111 #uuid "7e803a30-30a9-5665-9ad6-597fdeccf261" 13194139534610 true] [17592186298626 1034 "r=2" 13194139534610 true] [17592186298626 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534610 true] [17592186298626 1111 #uuid "219c9bda-c31c-575b-8c4d-511748675442" 13194139534610 true] [17592186298627 1034 "z=2" 13194139534610 true] [17592186298627 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534610 true] [17592186298627 1111 #uuid "dcf5e303-ad49-57f4-b254-6349f100e658" 13194139534610 true] [17592186298628 1034 "\\theta =2" 13194139534610 true] [17592186298628 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534